From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 17:10:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Show a folder's own icon from its .directory file

A folder with a .directory file (the KDE/Dolphin convention) shows the
icon named by Icon= in its [Desktop Entry] group, in the grid and list
views and as <name>-symbolic in the sidebar. Icon= takes a theme icon
name or an absolute path to an image of at most 1 MB; a name missing
from the theme falls back to the folder icon, and relative paths are
ignored.

Only the first 4 KB are read. Folders on remote, FUSE and automount
file systems are skipped, also when reached through a symlink. The
result is cached per folder and checked against the file's size,
mtime, inode and ctime, so an edited .directory shows on the next
listing. The logic lives in src/dir_icon.rs; folder_icon and
folder_icon_symbolic get a three-line hook each.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

